<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Albanian translation.

    English, in `values/`, is the source language (SPEC §9); this file is a
    translation of it and is kept complete. The rules are the ones that hold
    everywhere: positional placeholders, <plurals> for anything that agrees in
    number, and the `name` attributes left untouched.

    The typography is Albanian: quotation marks are „ … “, and the diacritics
    ë and ç are written in full — a bare e in place of an ë makes another word
    (mëso / meso, të / te). The dash that breaks a sentence is – with a space
    on either side, not the em dash the English file uses; it replaces that
    dash inside sentences (`welcome_data_body`, the four `journey_walk_*`
    lines) as well as inside `city_label`, the one format-only string that
    carries one. The only em dash left is `counterpart_none`, a glyph standing
    in for an absent figure rather than punctuation. The apostrophe, where the
    language needs one (t’i, ta, s’ka) or a network's name carries one
    (Vélib’), is ’ (U+2019) and never the straight quote, which is why nothing
    here is escaped.

    The reader is addressed in the second person singular, which is what
    Android's own Albanian does: of the 5 900 system strings extracted from a
    phone's `framework-res.apk` and `Settings.apk`, over two hundred use it —
    Provo përsëri, Kontrollo lidhjen dhe provo përsëri, Zgjidh një llogari,
    Trokit për ta ndryshuar — against a single line in the polite plural.
    Buttons take the same imperative: Vazhdo, Anulo, Fshi, Kapërce, Shfaq,
    Zëvendëso. Where the English is impersonal — "No history is kept", "It is
    read from the feed" — Albanian keeps it impersonal with the non-active
    voice (nuk ruhet, lexohet), and never says "we".

    The definite article is a suffix here, so a sentence built around a
    placeholder cannot control how the placeholder ends. Several lines are
    turned around rather than given an ending they could not answer for: what
    arrives follows a colon (`city_installed`, `storage_total`,
    `dataset_delete_description`, `station_address_nearby`), or a noun this
    file owns carries the article while the placeholder stands beside it
    (`city_here_body`, `city_proposal_body`). The three dataset names are all
    singular for the same reason, since `dataset_imported`, `dataset_deleted`
    and `dataset_delete_body` conjugate a verb with them.

    Plural categories are Albanian's two: `one` is the number 1 and nothing
    else, `other` is everything else, 0 included.

    See docs/glossary/sq.md for the words this file holds to, and
    CONTRIBUTING.md to submit a translation.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <string name="app_name">Roue Libre</string>

    <!-- Main screen: the station list. -->
    <string name="stations_title">Stacionet</string>

